    "created_at": "2026-11-12T10:05:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T10:05:19Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/547-electrode-from-faces · PR #1156 (draft, stacked on #1136 → #1131 → #560 → #551) · pinned by `sinker_electrode_tests` and `sinker_electrode_fuzz` (camcraft-motion), `sinker_electrode` and `sinker_electrode_mcp` (camcraft-app) · merges at the next cut\n\nWhat landed: `ElectrodeFromFaces` (undoable) and the MCP tool `electrode_from_faces`. A pocket's floor and walls yield an electrode tool (#541's kind), offset inward by the undersize (stated, or read from a machine condition) plus an optional orbit radius, standing a stated stub above the cavity's mouth. The generated rough and finish electrodes burn the pocket clean in the program verdict.\n\nScope held back, by name: the stock sim's box atom burns a rectangular face only, so a cavity that is not an axis-aligned rectangle (rounded corners, rotated, L-shaped, curved or drafted walls, a stepped floor) is refused, and the refusal names the follow-up, #1152 (a sim atom and tool record for an electrode body). No GUI entry yet: that is #548's page.\n\nLabels (this account cannot set them): swap `claimed` for `in-review`.\n",
